Jonquil ports and adapts DrClojure by Kim Taegyoon
(https://github.com/kimtg/DrClojure-Neo), distributed under the Eclipse
Public License 1.0. Code lifted from DrClojure keeps its original copyright,
and UPSTREAM.md lists which files it is in.

Jonquil's inspector view code (src/jonquil/inspect/view.clj) is lifted from
clojure-cli.repl (https://github.com/clojure/clojure-cli.repl), also
distributed under the Eclipse Public License 1.0. UPSTREAM.md records the
pinned commit and the changes.

Both were received under the Eclipse Public License 1.0. Jonquil distributes
them, with its own code, under the Eclipse Public License 2.0, as section 7 of
EPL-1.0 allows once a new version of the licence is published.

Six of Jonquil's colour themes take their colours from popular editor themes.
Jonquil uses their published colour values, mapped to its own token kinds in
src/jonquil/theme.clj, and includes none of their source. Each theme's
find-highlight tint is Jonquil's own, and any other colour that differs from
the original is noted beside its theme:

- Gruvbox Dark and Light: Gruvbox by morhetz, MIT/X11
  (https://github.com/morhetz/gruvbox, colors/gruvbox.vim).
- Dracula: Dracula Theme, MIT
  (https://github.com/dracula/emacs, dracula-theme.el).
- Nord: Nord by Sven Greb, MIT (https://github.com/nordtheme/nord,
  src/nord.css, and the comment colour from https://github.com/nordtheme/vim).
- Zenburn: the original Zenburn by Jani Nurminen (GNU GPL), with the palette
  as https://github.com/bbatsov/zenburn-emacs publishes it.
- Monokai: the original Monokai by Wimer Hazenberg, with the palette as
  https://github.com/oneKelvinSmith/monokai-emacs publishes it.

Six more themes take their colours the same way:

- Tokyo Night: tokyonight.nvim by folke, Apache-2.0
  (https://github.com/folke/tokyonight.nvim, lua/tokyonight/colors/night.lua
  and storm.lua).
- Catppuccin Mocha and Latte: Catppuccin, MIT, copyright 2021 Catppuccin
  (https://github.com/catppuccin/palette, palette.json).
- One Dark: onedark.vim by Joshua Dick, MIT
  (https://github.com/joshdick/onedark.vim, autoload/onedark.vim). Its
  comment grey is Jonquil's #666f7e, a little lighter than the original
  #5c6370, so that it meets Jonquil's contrast floor.
- Kanagawa: kanagawa.nvim by Tommaso Laurenzi, MIT
  (https://github.com/rebelot/kanagawa.nvim, lua/kanagawa/colors.lua).
- Rosé Pine: Rosé Pine, MIT
  (https://github.com/rose-pine/neovim, lua/rose-pine/palette.lua).

Jonquil's Parinfer engine (src/jonquil/parinfer.clj), lifted from DrClojure,
implements Parinfer v3.13.1 after parinfer.js
(https://github.com/parinfer/parinfer.js), and its test cases
(test-resources/parinfer/*.json) are parinfer.js's own. parinfer.js is
Copyright (c) 2015 Shaun Williams and contributors and distributed under the
MIT License, whose full text is in licenses/parinfer.js-LICENSE.md.

These libraries are compiled into Jonquil's binary:

- rewrite-edn (https://github.com/borkdude/rewrite-edn), which Jonquil uses
  to edit settings.edn. Copyright (c) 2021 - 2022 Michiel Borkent.
  Eclipse Public License 1.0.
- rewrite-clj 1.3.59 (https://github.com/clj-commons/rewrite-clj), which
  rewrite-edn is built on. Copyright (c) 2013-2018 Yannick Scherer. MIT
  License, full text in licenses/rewrite-clj-LICENSE.md.
- tools.reader 1.6.0 (https://github.com/clojure/tools.reader), which
  rewrite-clj uses. Copyright (c) Nicola Mometto, Rich Hickey &
  contributors. Eclipse Public License 1.0.
- data.json 2.5.1 (https://github.com/clojure/data.json). Copyright (c)
  Stuart Sierra, 2012. Eclipse Public License 1.0.
- time (https://github.com/jolt-lang/time), Jolt's java.time library.
  Eclipse Public License 2.0, the same as Jonquil's (see LICENSE).
- time-literals (https://github.com/henryw374/time-literals), whose data
